# Bold ways, stage A: second ways added after the first reading (10-19), so the ways offered come out even by colour.
# Each sits on a most-asked life event that had one bold way. No links: second ways end where they are.

# ================================================================ a season of bad air

== bold: a season of bad air / G
base: take the family to the relatives in the hills until the haze lifts
likelier_if: has [family who will always take you in] +10; has [old family name] +5
- G | move the family up to the hills for good, and live off the land there | v: tradition, security | act: move the family up to the hills for good, and live off the land there | chance: 40 | grants: growing food | drops_if_fails: kind:career
works: Up in the hills {N} learns to work the old family plot, and by autumn the household eats what {N} grows.
works: The air is clean, the garden comes good, and {N} has a patch of earth and the know-how to keep it.
fails: The hills have no work and the plot will not feed them, and the job {N} left in town is gone for good.
fails: The move falls apart in the first winter, and {N} comes back down to town with no job to go back to.

# ================================================================ earning a qualification

== bold: earning a qualification / G
base: put the paper away in a drawer; the work matters, not the certificate
likelier_if: has [good name in town] +10; has [old family name] +5
- G | give up your job and go home to teach at the old school | v: tradition, benevolence | act: give up their job and go home to teach at the old school, for a teacher's pay | chance: 35 | grants: teaching | drops_if_fails: kind:career
works: The old school takes {N} on, and by spring {N} is teaching the children of the street what {N} learned.
works: {N} turns out to have a gift for it, and the classes at the old school fill up within the year.
fails: The post at the school falls through in the summer, and the job {N} gave up has already been filled.
fails: The old school cannot pay after all, and {N} is left with neither the post nor the job left behind.

# ================================================================ a dry year on the land

== bold: a dry year on the land / G
base: help the family grow only what the dry land will carry this year
likelier_if: has [growing food] +10; has [old family name] +5
- G | get the neighbours to pool their water and work every field together until the rain | v: universalism, tradition | act: get the neighbours to pool their water and work every field together until the rain | chance: 35 | grants: neighbour who has your back | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: The street keeps every field alive between them, and from then on the neighbours look out for {N}.
works: The shared water sees the valley through to the rain, and the people next door count {N} as one of their own.
fails: The pooled water turns to quarrels, and {N} walks out of the village committees and clubs that autumn.
fails: One farm takes more than its share, the plan breaks up in shouting, and {N} gives up every place in the village groups.

# ================================================================ a parent dies

== bold: a parent dies / W
base: keep every funeral custom, and stand beside the family the whole day
likelier_if: has [savings] +10; has [reliable record] +5
- W | promise at the funeral to pay every debt they left, to the last coin | v: conformity, benevolence | act: promise at the funeral to pay every debt the parent left, to the last coin | chance: 30 | grants: good name in town | title_if_fails: bankruptcy or insolvency in their history
works: Over two hard years {N} pays off every debt, and the town speaks of {N} as someone whose word holds.
works: The last creditor is paid, and people in town say there is nobody more honest than {N}.
fails: The debts are bigger than anyone knew, and in the end {N} has to go through the courts as insolvent.
fails: {N} keeps paying until there is nothing left, and the court declares {N} insolvent.

# ================================================================ an unexpected chance: a grant, a role, a stage

== bold: an unexpected chance: a grant, a role, a stage / W
base: accept, and work every day to deserve the honour
likelier_if: mark 'kept your word' +10
- W | accept, and give your word to stay on and serve the place for three years after | v: conformity, benevolence | act: accept, and give their word to stay on and serve the place for three years after | chance: 30 | requires: reliable record | grants: trusted with the keys | takes_if_fails: reliable record
works: {N} keeps the promise year after year, and in the end the place hands {N} its keys and its trust.
works: The three years pass without a day missed, and {N} is the one they trust to open up and lock up.
fails: Halfway through, {N} cannot keep the promise and leaves early, and the place says so in its reference.
fails: The second year goes badly, {N} walks out, and the people who chose {N} say it plainly to anyone who asks.
